Package: kernelguard
Architecture: amd64
Depends: dkms (>= 2.8), ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: linux-headers-generic | linux-headers-amd64 | linux-headers
Suggests: curl, mailutils | bsd-mailx, bsdutils
Description: kernel-side attack and tamper detection: kernel module, monitor and escalation policy
 KernelGuard watches the running kernel for cache side-channel patterns,
 unauthorised keyboard handlers and DMA-capable devices, and kernel text, IDT
 and control-register tampering, and reports through an authenticated
 kernel-to-user channel.
 .
 This package installs the kernel module as DKMS source (it is rebuilt for
 every installed kernel and is not loaded automatically), the kgmon monitor
 with a systemd unit and a udev rule, and an example escalation policy with
 wall, webhook and mail actions.
 .
 The module is Ring 0 code and defaults to detect-only. Read
 /usr/share/doc/kernelguard/README.md before loading it, and try it in a
 virtual machine first. It is experimental.
